# The app needs none of these to run.
#
# Rainfall, air quality, the map and all scoring work with no configuration
# at all, because Open-Meteo is keyless and the register ships in the bundle.
# Copy this file to .env.local only if you want to switch on shared citizen
# reports.

# ── Shared citizen reports (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
#
# Without these, the Report tab still works: photos and GPS are captured and
# stored on the device, and nothing is uploaded anywhere. With them, reports
# are uploaded for review and appear to everyone once approved.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a project at https://supabase.com (free tier is enough)
#   2. Run supabase/schema.sql in the SQL editor
#   3. Copy Project URL and the anon key from Settings -> API
#   4. Create a moderator account under Authentication -> Users
#   5. Review submissions at /#moderate
#
# The anon key is public by design and safe in the client bundle. Every rule
# that matters is enforced by row level security in Postgres: an anonymous
# visitor can only insert a pending report, and can only read approved ones.
# Never put the service_role key here. That one bypasses every policy.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
